mono:
^[[1mgreet^[[0m 1.2.0  say hello

^[[1musage:^[[0m ^[[1mgreet^[[0m ^[[1m<name> [flags]^[[0m   greet someone
       ^[[1mgreet^[[0m ^[[1m--version^[[0m

^[[1mFlags^[[0m
  ^[[1m--shout^[[0m               in capitals
  ^[[1m--times^[[0m ^[[4m<n>^[[0m           say it n times
  ^[[1m--a-flag-past-the-column^[[0m ^[[4m<x>^[[0m  two spaces

^[[1mNotes^[[0m
  one line of prose
  ^[[4m/etc/greet.conf^[[0m
plain:
greet 1.2.0  say hello

usage: greet <name> [flags]   greet someone
       greet --version

Flags
  --shout               in capitals
  --times <n>           say it n times
  --a-flag-past-the-column <x>  two spaces

Notes
  one line of prose
  /etc/greet.conf
off paints nothing: true
mono dim is plain: true
